        },
        {
          "page": "7",
          "section": null,
          "quote": "Thus, the GB strengthening ability k obtained by fitting macro-yield strength increases with decreasing intrinsic SFE and increasing LFSS should be due to the weakened dislocation cross-slip ability. Hence, the higher GB strengthening ability of VCoNi MEA than that of the FCC metals, Cu–Al alloys, and some common HEA/MEA is attributed to the weakened cross-slip ability of dislocations caused by the high LFSS and relatively low intrinsic SFE of VCoNi MEA.",
          "table": null,
          "figure": null,
          "chunk_id": "d35fb6b54d7116eb:part:002"
        }
      ]
